        <title type="html">A new eye on the &lt;em&gt;Southern Sky&lt;/em&gt;</title>
        <id>urn:uuid:entry-001</id>
        <link rel="alternate" href="/stories/southern-sky"/>
        <published>2026-10-14T09:10:00Z</published>
        <updated>2026-10-14T12:00:00Z</updated>
        <author><name>Dr. Lina Ortega</name></author>
        <category term="Astronomy"/>
        <summary type="html">A survey telescope begins operations in Chile.</summary>
        <content type="xhtml">
            <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
                <p>The telescope will map faint galaxies across a huge area of sky.</p>
                <figure>
                    <img src="https://orbit.example.org/images/telescope.jpg" alt="Telescope dome"/>
                    <figcaption>The new survey telescope at dusk.</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <h2>Why it matters</h2>
                <p>Astronomers expect a flood of new data about dark energy.</p>
            </div>
        </content>
    </entry>
